# Declared ISOLATING so Gradle keeps incremental compilation on in every module this is applied to. Without this
# line Gradle reports "Full recompilation is required because StoragePolicyProcessor is not incremental" and
# recompiles the whole source set on any change.
#
# ISOLATING is the correct category here because the processor generates nothing: it only reports diagnostics, so
# there are no generated outputs to invalidate. It reads the supertypes of the type it checks, which is sound
# because Gradle already recompiles a class when its supertypes change, so a base losing its policy re-checks its
# subclasses.
bisq.network.storage_policy.StoragePolicyProcessor,ISOLATING
